{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/942352-recs-for-prince-valiant-or-king-arthur-pendragon-rpgs","id":942352,"title":"Recs for \"Prince Valiant\" or \"King Arthur Pendragon\" RPGs?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-02T17:55:47-07:00","id":942352,"title":"Recs for \"Prince Valiant\" or \"King Arthur Pendragon\" RPGs?","content":"Can anyone recommend the <b>Prince Valiant </b>or <b>King Arthur Pendragon</b> roleplaying games? There's a kickstarter going for a new edition, and - while I've heard the names before - I don't really know much about either game. Any thoughts? Strengths, weaknesses, cool ideas?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T22:45:26-07:00","id":942509,"title":"","content":"If it's the game I'm thinking of, then I've heard it is absolutely stellar at romance and emotional drama.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T09:17:29-07:00","id":944359,"title":"","content":"All I can tell you is Prince Valiant is an Old School Newsprint comic. First started printing about a year before Superman. I know fucking nothing of either RPG though, sorry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T14:50:47-07:00","id":946478,"title":"","content":"King Arthur Pendragon is almost unbeatable at what it aims for, simulating Medieval courtly romances. I personally felt like I understood the Feudal system and mindset a good bit better after playing it, since the game partially constrains you into playing a knight realistically, with the social expectations and etiquette common to the era, properly forcing the class structure rather than just being <i>asskicker with a helm.</i><br /> <br /> It's also the only RPG to accurately capture the feel of Celtic literature, in the sections on the Fairy realms and inhabitants.<br /> <br /> It has one massive campaign to accompany it, the Great Pendragon Campaign, where you basically play through <i>Le Morte d'Arthur.</i><br /> <br /> Possible negatives: you can really be only one class of character, a knight from Celtic Southern England (Logres) and the game does require some investment in immersing yourself in its atmosphere, i.e. you genuinely have to roleplay the characters for it to work well. These are positives for me, but just to mention them.<br /> <br /> There's a Charlemagne and Feudal Japan source books coming 2017-ish, if I remember correctly. If you've ever read <i>Lone Wolf and Cub</i> or other depictions of Feudal Japan, you can see the tropes are quite similar to Arthurian and Medieval literature, i.e. individuals constrained by their society and offering commentary on its contradictions, the stories often turning on the tension between society and the individual. <br /> <br /> Prince Valiant is a very simple RPG, I think it's really suited for children and teenagers as an intro to the hobby. The setting is very much the opposite of Pendragon's, i.e. the characters are modern, post-enlightenment individuals living in a medieval world, calling out its flaws, e.t.c. I'd have a read of some of the comic to see if you like it, as you'd really only be playing for the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3326-an-fhuiseog","name":"An Fhuiseog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3326_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}